-- title:
--   Multiplicativity of the Γ₁–⟨ T⟩ double-coset count in coprime levels
-- statement:
--   Let $M$ and $n$ be nonzero natural numbers that are coprime. For a level $N$, write $\pi_N$ for the reduction homomorphism $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z}) \to \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z}/N)$ obtained by applying the canonical ring homomorphism $\mathbb{Z} \to \mathbb{Z}/N$ entrywise (`Matrix.SpecialLinearGroup.map` of `Int.castRingHom`), and let $U_N = \pi_N(\Gamma_1(N))$ be the image of the congruence subgroup $\Gamma_1(N) \le \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ and $V_N = \pi_N(\langle T\rangle)$ the image of the cyclic subgroup generated by the standard unipotent matrix $T = \begin{pmatrix}1&1\\0&1\end{pmatrix}$, both regarded as subsets of $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z}/N)$. The assertion is an equality of cardinalities of the associated double-coset quotients: the number of double cosets $U_{Mn}\backslash \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z}/Mn) / V_{Mn}$ equals the product of the number of double cosets $U_M\backslash \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z}/M) / V_M$ with the number of double cosets $U_n\backslash \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z}/n) / V_n$. The cardinalities are taken as natural-number cardinalities of the double-coset quotient types.
--
--   The double-coset set $U_N\backslash \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z}/N)/V_N$ computes the cusps of the modular curve of level $\Gamma_1(N)$ up to the action of $\pm 1$, and this statement records that this count is multiplicative over coprime levels, reflecting the Chinese remainder decomposition $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z}/Mn) \cong \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z}/M) \times \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z}/n)$, under which $U_{Mn}$ and $V_{Mn}$ correspond to $U_M \times U_n$ and $V_M \times V_n$. It is used in the computation of the index of $\Gamma_1$ and of the cusp count at a level of the form (prime power times a coprime part), via [`CongruenceSubgroup.index_gamma1_mul_and_natCard_doubleCoset_gamma1_mul_of_prime_of_not_dvd`](thm.html#CongruenceSubgroup.index_gamma1_mul_and_natCard_doubleCoset_gamma1_mul_of_prime_of_not_dvd).
